      en: "Jabal Shammar is a mountain region in northern Saudi Arabia, part of the Hijaz range. Named after the Shammar tribe, the mountains reach 1,350 meters in height and are composed of sandstone and granite. The area is characterized by unique rock formations and deep canyons. The city of Hail, at the base, was a historic crossroads for pilgrimage and trade caravans. The climate is semiarid, with sparse acacia and shrub vegetation. The Jubbah rock art, a UNESCO World Heritage site, is located nearby.",
