      en: "The Midian Mountains (Jibal Midian) are located in northwestern Saudi Arabia, near the Gulf of Aqaba. Composed of granite and sandstone, the range rises to 2,120 meters at Jabal Qada'ah. The rugged peaks and deep canyons are the result of millennia of erosion. Historically, the region was known for copper mining, dating back to biblical times. Vegetation is sparse, with acacia and shrubs. Wildlife includes mountain ibex and birds of prey. The area attracts hikers and climbers seeking remote wilderness.",
