      en: "Wadi ad-Dawasir is a major wadi in southern Saudi Arabia, flowing from the Sarawat Mountains into the Rub al-Khali. It is about 350 km long and serves as a vital agricultural region. The town of Wadi ad-Dawasir is the administrative hub. The valley's groundwater reserves support large-scale irrigation for wheat, dates, and vegetables. Historically, the Incense Route passed through this wadi. The climate is hyper-arid, with less than 50 mm of rainfall per year. Vegetation is limited to the wadi banks and irrigated farms.",
